# Part of Hyperdrive recipes, https://github.com/Hyperdrive-Project/recipes
# Apache-2.0. If this helps you, a credit to Hyperdrive recipes is appreciated.
# RECIPE (docs/RECIPES.md): docker build --build-arg NHD_STACK=v3 -t nemotron-hyperdrive:1.4.0rc1-v3 .
#   scripts/make_fp4_mamba.sh
#   IMAGE=nemotron-hyperdrive:1.4.0rc1-v3 MODEL=super-vl-nvfp4-m4 scripts/serve.sh configs/b300/hyperdrive-b300-v3.yaml configs/b300/hyperdrive-b300-v3.env
# Paths below are the image's (/opt/nhd, /models, /cache).
# Hyperdrive on B300, v3 (2026-11-02 afternoon): v2 (hyperdrive-b300-v2.env, same yaml: hyperdrive-b300-v2.yaml) plus
# FP4 Mamba-2 projections. The 80 Mamba-2 projections (in_proj + out_proj of 40 layers) are re-quantized from the checkpoint's own static
# FP8 to NVFP4 (W4A4, 16-element block scales, the layout the checkpoint's experts use). A model change,
# kept because the reasoning-on quality gate held: math 49/50, code 29/30, tools 11/11 (v2: 48/50, 29/30,
# 11/11; original model 49/50, 29/30, 11/11). Paired A/B on one B300, 160 users, 8K in / 1K out, unique prompts (job
# m4e-ab): burst 6,363 -> 6,800 (+6.9%), sustained 6,338 -> 6,661 (+5.1%), prefill-only 85.1K -> 98.0K input tok/s,
# decode-only 14,452 -> 14,240. That pod ran v2 ~6% below the morning pod (6,752 / 6,723), so compare within a pod.
# Measured on the morning pod (2026-11-02 1:27 PM PST, job v3o-ab, October config then v3 back to back, same protocol):
# October config 5,679 burst / 5,422 sustained, v3 7,264 / 7,053 (+27.9% / +30.1%; +7.6% / +4.9% over v2's 6,752 / 6,723
# on that pod this morning).
# Make the weights once (GPU, ~1 min): python3 tools/m4_convert.py <NVFP4 checkpoint> <DST>
#   --targets in_proj,out_proj --mode overlay   (DST symlinks the shards and adds nhd-m4-overlay.st, ~2.3 GB; needs
#   patches/v3/weight-overlay.diff and NHD_WEIGHT_OVERLAY below)   or --mode full (a standalone checkpoint
#   with the affected shards rewritten, which should load on stock TRT-LLM without the overlay patch; untested).
# Serve DST as the model. TRT-LLM 1.4.0rc1 reads the NVFP4 entries from hf_quant_config.json; the RMSNorm in front of
# each projection fuses the FP4 activation quantize, so NHD_F5 and NHD_MAMBA_NORM_FP8 (FP8-only) step aside by themselves.
#
# v2 below, unchanged:
# Hyperdrive on B300, v2 (2026-11-02): the B300 env (hyperdrive-b300.env) plus the overnight kernels. Needs, on top of
# patches/hyperdrive/03 04 06 07: patches/v3/cake-ssd.diff, conv-triton.diff, mamba-norm-fp8.diff (and
# guided-skip.diff for NHD_GUIDED_SKIP), and the FlashInfer main e74a167 CAKE SSD sources (the v3 image has all of these:
# Dockerfile NHD_STACK=v3, sources in /opt/nhd/fimain-e74a167). Config: hyperdrive-b300-v2.yaml.
# Vision path (patch 05; not used by the text-only runs this was measured with).
NHD_VISION_ATTN_BACKEND=TRTLLM
# F5 needs patch 03 and NHD_MK_DIR=<repo>/patches/hyperdrive (the directory holding nhd_mk).
NHD_PREFILL_GRAPH_TEXT_ONLY=2
NHD_SSD_FUSED_SCAN=1
NHD_SSD_FUSED_STATE=1
NHD_F5=1
# CAKE Mamba2 SSD prefill (FlashInfer main, cu_seqlens form). D=1 x skip is added by our Triton pass on calls with
# initial states (D with initial states gave wrong outputs in our call path; FlashInfer alone checks out, j26b/j26c).
NHD_SSD_CAKE=1
NHD_CAKE_FORM=cu
NHD_CAKE_D_MODE=split
NHD_CAKE_FI_DIR=/opt/nhd/fimain-e74a167
NHD_CAKE_JIT_DIR=/cache/nhd_cake_jit_main
# Triton varlen causal conv1d for the Mamba2 prefill, B300-tuned tile (B200: 1x16x256x4).
NHD_CONV_TRITON=1
NHD_CONV_TILE=1x32x128x4
# Mamba2 gated RMSNorm writes FP8 straight into the FP8 out_proj.
NHD_MAMBA_NORM_FP8=1
# Skip the no-op guided-decoding host functions and GPU drains in steps without a structured-output request.
NHD_GUIDED_SKIP=1

# FP4 Mamba projections (v3): the converted tensors, applied after the checkpoint's shards (weight-overlay.diff).
NHD_WEIGHT_OVERLAY=/models/super-vl-nvfp4-m4/nhd-m4-overlay.st
